Effective Date: August 14, 2026

This End User License Agreement ("Agreement") is between High Agency, Inc. ("we," "us," or "our") and you ("you" or "user"). It covers your installation and use of the pen.dev software.

1. License grant

We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use pen.dev for your personal or professional use, subject to this Agreement. If we introduce paid or enterprise features, those features may be subject to additional terms or a separate written agreement.

Distribution via third-party registries. pen.dev is distributed as a desktop application, as extensions for IDE/editor environments (e.g., Cursor, VS Code), and as a command-line tool (CLI), and may be made available through third-party registries (e.g., Open VSX, VS Code/Cursor marketplaces, npm). Registry terms may also apply, and you must comply with them. Distribution via a registry does not grant any additional rights beyond this Agreement. Registries are not parties to this Agreement and have no obligation to provide support, maintenance, or warranties for the Software. We may update, suspend, or remove the Software from any registry at any time.

2. Account & authentication

The Software requires you to create an account and authenticate upon launch. This authentication exists solely to (a) validate that you hold an active license for the Software, and (b) verify your identity against the licensed account.

The only personal data transmitted to and stored on High Agency, Inc. servers in connection with your account is your email address, your name, a username, and your password credentials (transmitted over encrypted channels). No Inputs, Outputs, or other user content is exchanged with our servers during or after authentication.

You are responsible for keeping your account credentials secure and for all activity under your account.

3. Restrictions

You may not:

Copy, modify, or redistribute pen.dev

Reverse-engineer or decompile the software

Rent, lease, or sublicense pen.dev to others

Use pen.dev in violation of any law or regulation

You must not scrape, crawl, bulk-export, or extract datasets from the Software or any outputs it produces, and you must not use the Software or outputs to develop, train, or improve any model or service that competes with ours, except under a separate written agreement with High Agency, Inc. Do not submit or process high-risk data (including payment card data, bank or government ID numbers, health information, biometric identifiers/templates, precise geolocation, minors' data, or GDPR special-category data) without our prior written consent and appropriate safeguards.

4. Ownership

Software. pen.dev and all related materials are owned by High Agency, Inc. This Agreement does not give you ownership — only the right to use the Software under the license terms. The Software is licensed, not sold. Certain paid or enterprise features may be subject to a separate written commercial agreement. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

Inputs. You retain ownership of any content you create or submit through pen.dev ("Inputs"). Inputs from text-based AI features used with your own provider accounts are exchanged directly between your device and third-party AI providers and do not pass through High Agency, Inc. servers. To the limited extent any technical processing on our infrastructure is necessary to facilitate pen.dev Pro models or image, SVG, and stock image features, you grant us a limited, non-exclusive license for that sole purpose.

Outputs. As between you and us, you own the AI-generated outputs produced for you ("Outputs"), subject to any third-party rights. Because Outputs are generated by the underlying third-party AI provider, you should also review the applicable provider's terms of service. We do not guarantee that Outputs are unique or non-infringing, and you are responsible for reviewing and using them lawfully.

Model training. Inputs and Outputs from text-based AI features used with your own provider accounts are exchanged directly between your device and third-party AI providers and do not pass through our servers; we have no access to them and do not train any models on them. Where you use pen.dev Pro models, we do not use your Inputs or Outputs to train AI models; processing by our inference partners is governed by our agreements with them. The third-party AI provider's model training and data use practices are governed by their own terms.

5. Feedback

If you voluntarily provide suggestions, ideas, or feedback about the Software, you grant High Agency, Inc. a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, modify, and incorporate them into the Software and our services. This license does not extend to any confidential information you mark as such in writing, or to Inputs or Outputs themselves (which remain governed by Section 4).

6. Updates

We may provide updates or improvements to pen.dev. These may install automatically or require your approval, depending on your settings.

The Software may send minimal diagnostics/usage data necessary to operate and secure the product, as described in our Privacy Policy. Such diagnostics/usage data does not include user Inputs or generated Outputs (no prompts, no generated content, no source code).

Text-based AI features using your own provider accounts. Inputs and Outputs from text-based AI features used with your own provider accounts (e.g., code generation, design assistance, chat completions via Anthropic, OpenAI, or GitHub Copilot) are exchanged directly between your device and the relevant third-party AI provider. They do not pass through, and are not stored, recorded, logged, or cached on, High Agency, Inc. servers at any time.

pen.dev Pro models (when available). If you choose a pen.dev-provided AI model, your Inputs and Outputs are routed from your device through our inference partners using service credentials provisioned by High Agency, Inc. This content is not stored, recorded, logged, or cached on our servers, and we do not use it to train AI models.

Image and SVG generation features. Image- and SVG-related features operate differently. Requests and any content you intentionally submit are transmitted through High Agency, Inc. servers to the relevant third-party provider. This transmission is the minimum technically necessary to fulfill your request. We do not store, record, log, or cache this content on our servers — it is forwarded to the third-party provider in real time and not retained.

Any local storage of Inputs or Outputs occurs solely on your device (e.g., browser localStorage or OS filesystem) for your convenience.

7. Disclaimer

pen.dev is provided "as is" and "as available." You are solely responsible for reviewing, validating, and deciding whether to use any outputs or suggestions.

We make no warranties regarding its performance, accuracy, availability, or reliability. pen.dev may use AI models to generate content or suggestions. AI outputs can be imperfect, biased, or unexpected. We don't guarantee that any output is accurate, appropriate, or fit for a particular purpose.

Do not rely on the Software or its outputs in safety-critical or life-critical contexts (e.g., medical or clinical use, emergency services, aviation, automotive control systems, industrial control, energy, defense), or in any scenario where failure could result in personal injury, death, or significant property or environmental damage.

Third-party AI providers (your own accounts). The Software enables your device to connect directly to third-party AI providers (such as Anthropic, OpenAI, or GitHub Copilot) using your own provider accounts to generate content or suggestions. These services are governed by the applicable provider's terms of service and privacy policies, and we are not responsible for their performance, availability, content, or data handling practices.

pen.dev Pro models (when available). Where you use pen.dev Pro models, content is routed through our inference partners as described in our Privacy Policy. We do not guarantee the performance or availability of any AI model.

Third-party image, SVG, and stock content services. Certain features use third-party services to generate or source images and SVG graphics, including Google Gemini, OpenAI, Quiver AI, and Unsplash. We may change or add providers over time. Image and SVG generation features operate differently from text-based AI features: your request and any content you intentionally submit are transmitted through High Agency, Inc. servers to the relevant third-party provider in real time and are not stored, recorded, logged, or cached on our servers. For stock image search (Unsplash), pen.dev's agent generates search queries derived from your project context; your prompts are not transmitted verbatim to Unsplash. Third-party services and content are subject to their own terms (including any attribution or usage requirements), and we disclaim responsibility for third-party content and do not guarantee its accuracy, legality, availability, or non-infringement.

